#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0033 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "⚠ RE-CUT 2026-09-08 (R-4.12 hoist): expect moved noViolation -> skipped. `var_exists(TV.VISITNUM)` was a top-level conjunct, so an absent TV made the whole AND false and the rule reported a SILENT ZERO -- which is what this scenario used to pin. It is now Requirements.Variables.All ["TV.VISITNUM"], so the rule is gated out and reports SKIPPED naming the variable. Same violations either way; only the status channel moves, which is R-4.11's whole argument. If this EXECUTES again the entry was dropped -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin. PRIOR NOTE: Fix #246 flood arm: TV is absent entirely, so $tv_visitnum is the empty set and is_not_contained_by would be vacuously true on every planned populated VISITNUM - before the top-level TV.VISITNUM exists guard this fixture flooded (both rows fired). The guard resolves TV through the dataset resolver, finds nothing, and suppresses the rule with no finding."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 2  | BASELINE
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB | 99 | WEEK 99
---

dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVPRESP  type=Char label="Pre-Specified"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 2  | BASELINE | Y
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 99 | WEEK 99  | Y
---
